Z||000001||stimpy||02-27-2001||11:20 PM||||Why would you need to order fiberfill over the net? Just go down to the local yardage store and by a bag of it. Also known as batting. I probably would not want to use fberglass insulation, too dense, plus I'd be concerned about loose glass fibers cutting up my speaker. ||||reg||5
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||02-27-2001||11:25 PM||||The product is called "Handi Foam" It's a expanding polyuerthane foam (spray can).<BR>DAP also makes the same type product (KWIK FOAM) You should be able to get it at any hardware??<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||4
Z||000003||1FST2M6||02-28-2001||08:27 AM||||special order? take a pillow cut it open and use that. it's the same thing you just aren't paying for a name brand.<P>oh make sure it's not a feather pillow.. the expanding foam solidifys and will not produce the same dampening effect as the poly-fil or pulled-polyester pillow stuffing. available at any Wal-mart K-mart, 3D, not sure what else you have Canada but your surley don't have to special order it. any arts/crafts store, fabric store should have it too... <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-28-2001).]||||reg||1
