Z||000012||MontanaFiero||03-02-2001||02:38 AM||||NO NO NO... Don't use the stuff in your pillow!  Go to your local radio shack and buy accoustical fiberglass insulation. It is about one inch thick and is DESIGNED for speaker enclosures. It has the correct sound absorbtion qualities, and it won't blow out the vent of the speaker box and make a mess like "pillow stuffing"<P>You are probably building a "sealed" enclosure if you are doing this in a fiero, so staple (or glue) some of this to the <B>back, top and one side</B> of the enclosure and it will be perfect.<P>The can of expanding foam??? I think once that stuff dries it might reflect too much sound. The idea is to absorb or "dampen" the sound so the bass in not so "boomy". More is not necessarily better. In boxes with ports the amount of fiberglass is actually calculated. So just put the amount I described above and it should sound just fine.<P>Oh, and make sure you use a crossover on your speaker or an amp that has a "low pass filter" switch.<P><P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||4
